module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SiteDividedPowerDifferentials
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.BaseChangeIsomorphism
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Crystalline.SmallSite.ModuleCohomology

/-!
# The crystalline differentials `Ω_{X/S}` and `d_{X/S}` on the small crystalline site

Fix a global crystalline situation `(p, (S, I, γ), X)` of [Stacks, Tag 07MF].  [Stacks, Tag 07IW]
applies its construction of the universal divided power derivation of a sheaf of rings on a site
to the structure morphism `(X/S)_cris ⟶ Sh(S_Zar)` and obtains the universal divided power
derivation
```
d_{X/S} : 𝒪_{X/S} ⟶ Ω_{X/S}
```
on the small crystalline site `Cris(X/S)`, whose divided power derivations are the
`S`-derivations of [Stacks, Tag 07IX].  This file carries that out with the general construction
`Crystalline.siteDPDifferentials` of `SiteDividedPowerDifferentials.lean`.

The data entering the construction are:

* the structure sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of `Cris(X/S)`, `SmallSite.commStructureSheaf`, sending
  `(U, T, δ)` to `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`;
* the divided power ideal `𝒥_{X/S}`, sending `(U, T, δ)` to the ideal of global sections of the
  divided power ideal of `T`, with its divided powers `δ`; the transition maps are homomorphisms
  of divided power rings because the morphisms of `Cris(X/S)` are morphisms of divided power
  schemes (`crisDividedPowers`);
* the base: the subring of `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)` generated by the sections pulled back from some open
  `V ⊆ S` receiving `T`, `crisBaseRing`.  It is the image of the inverse image `τ⁻¹𝒪_S` in
  `𝒪_{X/S}` on the level of presheaves, and an additive map satisfying the Leibniz rule kills it
  exactly when it kills those pulled back sections; so a divided power derivation relative to
  `crisBaseRing` is an `S`-derivation in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 07IX], which is
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.crisDerivation_d_base` together with
  `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite.crisDerivationMk`.

The objects of `Cris(X/S)` form a `Type (u + 1)`, so the sheaves of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules are taken
with sections in `Type (u + 1)`, the universe of the library's `SmallSite.ModuleSheaf`, where the
small crystalline site has sheafification.

## Main definitions

Everything lives in the namespace `Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite`.

* `crisBaseRing`, `crisBaseMap` — the base presheaf of rings and its map into `𝒪_{X/S}`.
* `crisDividedPowers` — the divided power ideal `𝒥_{X/S}` with its divided powers.
* `crisDifferentials` — the sheaf `Ω_{X/S}` of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules.
* `crisUniversalDerivation` — the universal divided power derivation `d_{X/S}`.
* `crisDerivationMk` — an `S`-derivation in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 07IX], as a derivation
  relative to `crisBaseMap`.

## Main results

* `existsUnique_crisDesc` — every `S`-derivation of `𝒪_{X/S}` into a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules
  factors through `d_{X/S}` by a unique map of sheaves of modules.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IW](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IW)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IX)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07IM](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07IM)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 07MF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07MF)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite AlgebraicGeometry

universe v u

namespace Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite

attribute [local instance] hasSheafCompose_forget₂_smallTopology

variable (S : GlobalCrystallineSituation.{u})

/-- The structure sheaf `𝒪_{X/S}` of `Cris(X/S)` as a sheaf of rings, over which the sheaves of
`𝒪_{X/S}`-modules below are taken. -/
abbrev crisStructureRingSheaf : Sheaf (smallTopology S) RingCat.{u} :=
  _root_.Crystalline.ringSheaf.{u, u, u + 1} (J := smallTopology S) (commStructureSheaf S)

/-- The ring of sections of `𝒪_{X/S}` over an object of `Cris(X/S)` is the ring of global sections
of its ambient scheme. -/
theorem commStructureSheaf_obj_obj (X : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ) :
    (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X = Γ(X.unop.obj.thickening.target.scheme, ⊤) := rfl

/-- The sections of `𝒪_{X/S}` pulled back from an open of the base are sent to such sections
by the transition maps. -/
theorem crisBase_map_mem {X Y : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ} (k : X ⟶ Y)
    {s : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X} (hs : s ∈ crysBaseSections S X.unop.obj) :
    (commStructureSheaf S).obj.map k s ∈ crysBaseSections S Y.unop.obj :=
  map_mem_crysBaseSections S k.unop.hom hs

/-- The transition maps of `𝒪_{X/S}` carry the subring generated by the pulled back sections into
the subring generated by the pulled back sections. -/
theorem crisBase_closure_le {X Y : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ} (k : X ⟶ Y) :
    Subring.closure (crysBaseSections S X.unop.obj) ≤
      (Subring.closure (crysBaseSections S Y.unop.obj)).comap
        ((commStructureSheaf S).obj.map k).hom :=
  Subring.closure_le.mpr fun _ hs ↦ Subring.subset_closure (crisBase_map_mem S k hs)

/-- **The base presheaf of rings of `Cris(X/S)`**: over `(U, T, δ)` the subring of `Γ(T, 𝒪_T)`
generated by the sections pulled back from some open `V ⊆ S` receiving `T`. -/
def crisBaseRing : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat.{u} where
  obj X := CommRingCat.of (Subring.closure (crysBaseSections S X.unop.obj))
  map k := CommRingCat.ofHom (((commStructureSheaf S).obj.map k).hom.restrict _ _
    fun _ hx ↦ crisBase_closure_le S k hx)
  map_id X := by
    ext x
    exact congrArg (fun g ↦ g x.1) ((commStructureSheaf S).obj.map_id X)
  map_comp k l := by
    ext x
    exact congrArg (fun g ↦ g x.1) ((commStructureSheaf S).obj.map_comp k l)

/-- The inclusion of the base presheaf of rings into `𝒪_{X/S}`. -/
def crisBaseMap : crisBaseRing S ⟶ (commStructureSheaf S).obj where
  app X := (CommRingCat.ofHom (Subring.subtype _) :
    (crisBaseRing S).obj X ⟶ (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X)
  naturality _ _ _ := by
    ext
    rfl

/-- **The divided power ideal `𝒥_{X/S}` of `Cris(X/S)` with its divided powers**: over
`(U, T, δ)` the ideal of global sections of the divided power ideal of `T`, with the divided
powers `δ`. -/
def crisDividedPowers : PresheafDividedPowers (commStructureSheaf S).obj where
  ideal X := sectionIdeal X.unop.obj.thickening.target.scheme.sheaf
    X.unop.obj.thickening.target.ideal (op ⊤)
  dividedPowers X := crysDividedPowers S X.unop.obj
  naturality k := k.unop.hom.targetHom.compatible ⊤

/-! ### `S`-derivations -/

/-- A derivation of `𝒪_{X/S}` relative to the base presheaf kills every section pulled back from
an open of `S`. -/
theorem crisDerivation_d_base {M : PresheafOfModules.{v} (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj}
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M (crisBaseMap S))
    {X : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ}
    {s : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X} (hs : s ∈ crysBaseSections S X.unop.obj) :
    D.d s = 0 :=
  D.d_app (X := X) ⟨s, Subring.subset_closure hs⟩

/-- An additive map satisfying the Leibniz rule kills the subring generated by a set it kills. -/
theorem eq_zero_of_mem_closure {R : Type u} [Ring R] {N : Type v} [AddCommGroup N]
    [Module R N] (d : R →+ N) (hmul : ∀ a b : R, d (a * b) = a • d b + b • d a) {Z : Set R}
    (hZ : ∀ s ∈ Z, d s = 0) {x : R} (hx : x ∈ Subring.closure Z) : d x = 0 := by
  have h1 : d 1 = 0 := by
    have := hmul 1 1
    rw [mul_one, one_smul] at this
    simpa using this
  induction hx using Subring.closure_induction with
  | mem s hs => exact hZ s hs
  | zero => exact d.map_zero
  | one => exact h1
  | add a b _ _ ha hb => rw [d.map_add, ha, hb, add_zero]
  | neg a _ ha => rw [d.map_neg, ha, neg_zero]
  | mul a b _ _ ha hb => rw [hmul, ha, hb, smul_zero, smul_zero, add_zero]

/-- **An `S`-derivation in the sense of [Stacks, Tag 07IX]** as a derivation relative to the base
presheaf: a natural family of additive maps on sections, satisfying the Leibniz rule and killing
every section pulled back from an open of `S`. -/
def crisDerivationMk {M : PresheafOfModules.{v} (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj}
    (d : ∀ X : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ,
      (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj.obj X →+ M.obj X)
    (hmul : ∀ X (a b : (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj.obj X),
      d X (a * b) = a • d X b + b • d X a)
    (hmap : ∀ {X Y : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ} (k : X ⟶ Y)
      (x : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X),
      d Y ((commStructureSheaf S).obj.map k x) = M.map k (d X x))
    (hbase : ∀ X (s : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X), s ∈ crysBaseSections S X.unop.obj →
      d X s = 0) :
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' M (crisBaseMap S) where
  d {X} := d X
  d_mul := hmul _
  d_map := hmap
  d_app {X} a := eq_zero_of_mem_closure (d X) (hmul X) (hbase X) a.2

/-- The derivation built by `crisDerivationMk` has the given maps on sections. -/
@[simp]
theorem crisDerivationMk_d {M : PresheafOfModules.{v} (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj}
    (d : ∀ X : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ,
      (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj.obj X →+ M.obj X)
    (hmul : ∀ X (a b : (crisStructureRingSheaf S).obj.obj X),
      d X (a * b) = a • d X b + b • d X a)
    (hmap : ∀ {X Y : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ} (k : X ⟶ Y)
      (x : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X),
      d Y ((commStructureSheaf S).obj.map k x) = M.map k (d X x))
    (hbase : ∀ X (s : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X), s ∈ crysBaseSections S X.unop.obj →
      d X s = 0) (X : (CrystallineThickening S)ᵒᵖ) (x : (commStructureSheaf S).obj.obj X) :
    (crisDerivationMk S d hmul hmap hbase).d x = d X x := rfl

/-! ### `Ω_{X/S}` and `d_{X/S}` -/


/-- **The sheaf `Ω_{X/S}` of crystalline differentials** on `Cris(X/S)`: the sheaf of divided power
differentials of `𝒪_{X/S}` relative to the base, with respect to `𝒥_{X/S}`. -/
def crisDifferentials : SheafOfModules.{u + 1} (crisStructureRingSheaf S) :=
  siteDPDifferentials.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u} (crisBaseMap S) (crisDividedPowers S)

/-- **The universal divided power derivation `d_{X/S} : 𝒪_{X/S} ⟶ Ω_{X/S}`.** -/
def crisUniversalDerivation :
    PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (crisDifferentials S).val (crisBaseMap S) :=
  siteDPUniversalDerivation.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u} (crisBaseMap S) (crisDividedPowers S)

/-- `d_{X/S}` obeys the divided power chain rule on the sections of `𝒥_{X/S}`. -/
theorem isSiteDPDerivation_crisUniversalDerivation :
    IsSiteDPDerivation.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u} (crisBaseMap S) (crisDividedPowers S)
      (crisUniversalDerivation S) :=
  isSiteDPDerivation_siteDPUniversalDerivation.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u} (crisBaseMap S)
    (crisDividedPowers S)

/-- **The universal property of `d_{X/S}`** ([Stacks, Tag 07IW]).  Every `S`-derivation of
`𝒪_{X/S}` into a sheaf of `𝒪_{X/S}`-modules on `Cris(X/S)`, that is every derivation killing the
sections pulled back from the opens of `S` and obeying the divided power chain rule on `𝒥_{X/S}`
([Stacks, Tag 07IX]), factors through `d_{X/S}` by a unique map of sheaves of modules. -/
@[stacks 07IW "Ω_{X/S} and the universal divided power derivation d_{X/S} : 𝒪_{X/S} → Ω_{X/S} on
  Cris(X/S), from the construction on a site applied to (X/S)_cris → Sh(S_Zar)"]
theorem existsUnique_crisDesc (F : SheafOfModules.{u + 1} (crisStructureRingSheaf S))
    (D : PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation' (M := F.val) (crisBaseMap S))
    (hD : IsSiteDPDerivation.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u} (M := F.val) (crisBaseMap S)
      (crisDividedPowers S) D) :
    ∃! f : crisDifferentials S ⟶ F, (crisUniversalDerivation S).postcomp f.val = D :=
  existsUnique_siteDPDesc.{u + 1, u + 1, u, u} (crisBaseMap S) (crisDividedPowers S) F D hD

end Crystalline.GlobalCrystallineSituation.SmallSite
